> > fd files are specifically excluded from most of the restrictions.
 
> This is good news, because it allows a cleaner interface for the Sauter
> fonts. I always felt the method I used before (employing fonttext.cfg and
> fontmath.cfg) was very clumsy.
 
It is essentially the same conditions on fd files as all the previous
releases.
 
The case of the Sauter fonts is a difficult one, as while probably a
good thing in principle, the current situation is that sites using
them are a very small minority and so dvi files produced are rather
non-portable. So it is probably a good idea to make this clear to
users by using a higher profile change than just switching the fd
files. (I do not have any definite suggestion, just musing at this
point...)
 
One solution would be to have a big push to get all/most sites to
switch to sauter fonts but this is unlikely to happen (and on texs
using type1 or true type fonts I am not sure they are even available?)
In any case the effort would probably be better spent getting the TeX
community to switch to the T1 encoding (How are the new  dc fonts
coming along? :-)
 
David

